# Compass UI guidance

The selected identity uses Compass cream-and-orange colours with Folio layouts: a cream desk, warm paper documents, orange actions, DM Sans controls and Newsreader narrative headings. Jules restored this palette on 9 September 2026. For incidental changes, reuse `src/app/folio.css` and `src/components/folio/`. The design contract is `docs/design/FOLIO.md`. Keep the restored colours and existing editorial typography; the earlier lilac-and-plum palette is superseded.

A request to improve UI or UX authorises relevant changes to hierarchy, spacing, layout, feedback, and interaction within the requested surface. Make the result meaningfully better and explain the evidence. It does not require preserving a demonstrated usability problem. Change the broader brand, theme, or navigation model only when that is within the requested scope.

For a review, recommend valuable changes even if implementation is a separate task. Separate verified defects from design proposals. Do not treat a checklist or a tool's preferred style as the verdict.

Inspect current sources when needed: `src/app/globals.css`, `tailwind.config.ts`, `src/components/ui/card.tsx`, `src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx`, `src/components/OperatorShell.tsx`, and `src/components/NavLinks.tsx`. Use their actual values rather than an old prose snapshot.
